+Direct zero-credential `/health` pull at ~06:08Z: `{"status": "healthy", "version": "2.0.0", "uptime_seconds": 16770.67}` → container booted ~01:30Z. The tower sweep still flagged it `update_failed` at 06:06–06:08Z. Staleness ≥ 4.6h on one node, with the same class already proven at 04:17Z (`uptime_seconds=9614`). Worker answers `"ok"` (vocabulary-compliant); tower body-`degraded` is at least partially self-referential (it degrades because it *sees* the stale flags it emits).
