+## Adjudication of #2009 (provider sentry pass 05:54Z)
+
+#2009 claims: "sweep polarity FLIPS — primary/worker recover, degraded flag moves to render-mcp".
+
+- **Half-true at the contract layer**: all 5 nodes serve on-contract health faces, so "recover" is real where it matters (the live edge).
+- **Refuted as a "move/flip"**: at 06:06–06:08Z the sweep flags all three of primary + worker + mcp simultaneously (`update_failed` ×3). Nothing moved; the flags are persistent and stale, not flapping between nodes.
+- **Correct model**: Render deployStatus metadata in the tower sweep is a stale cache, unreliable as a health signal for ≥4.6h stretches. The D4 contract probe — live edge, zero credential — is the reliable signal. This is exactly the failure mode WO #1874 predicted ("'deployed' must be gated by the LIVE edge contract, never by cached provider records") and why #1962 exists.
